<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greek language</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greek language is an Indo-European language with a written history stretching back over three thousand years. After the conquests of Alexander it became a common language of administration and culture across the Macedonian and Seleucid realms. It was the main language of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and was also used in inscriptions and coinage by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>.</p></div>
